From 4881be20a4b299ad28b1eec472cff1c5d9d076f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:31:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 73/85] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Clear DP AON toggle in USB4 mode

In USB4 mode, qmp_combo_com_init() clears only the USB4 AON toggle
enable. The Glymur USB4v2 PHY HSR also writes DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE = 0
in each of its USB4 DP tunneling clock sequences, but the driver never
does that when the PHY is in USB4 mode, so the DP toggle is left in
whatever state it was found in before DP is tunneled.

The non-USB4 branch also writes cfg->regs[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE]
unconditionally. That is fine for the layouts that provide it today, but
a layout that sets QPHY_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE without a DP offset would end
up clearing bit 0 of offset 0x0 instead, which is the USB3 AON clamp
enable register on v8 PHYs.

Clear the DP AON toggle as well when in USB4 mode, and only touch it in
either branch if the layout actually defines an offset for it.

Signed-off-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 21cf18e12aee..afd372123c43 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4667,9 +4667,12 @@ static int qmp_combo_com_init(struct qmp_combo *qmp, bool force)
 	if (aon_toggle) {
 		if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_USB4 && cfg->regs[QPHY_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE]) {
 			qphy_clrbits(aon_toggle, cfg->regs[QPHY_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE], 0x1);
+			if (cfg->regs[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE])
+				qphy_clrbits(aon_toggle, cfg->regs[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE], 0x1);
 		} else if (cfg->regs[QPHY_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE]) {
 			qphy_clrbits(aon_toggle, cfg->regs[QPHY_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE], 0x1);
-			qphy_clrbits(aon_toggle, cfg->regs[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE], 0x1);
+			if (cfg->regs[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE])
+				qphy_clrbits(aon_toggle, cfg->regs[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE], 0x1);
 		}
 	}
 
